.TH CONDUCTOR-IDP 8 "2026-10-03" "Samba Conductor" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
conductor-idp \- OpenID Connect and SAML identity provider backed by Samba AD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conductor-idp
.RB [ \-config
.IR FILE ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conductor-idp
authenticates users against Samba Active Directory and serves OpenID
Connect and SAML 2.0 to registered applications, with access granted per AD
group and the Samba Conductor second-factor policy. The service runs as the
.B conductor-idp
user, started by
.BR conductor-idp.service ;
its secrets (master key, service account password) are systemd credentials.
.PP
Run
.B conductor-idp
.I command
.B \-h
for a command's flags.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the provider.
.TP
.B client add|list|show|update|rotate|enable|disable|remove
Manage OpenID Connect clients.
.TP
.B saml add|list|show|update|enable|disable|remove
Manage SAML service providers.
.TP
.B keys list | keys rotate oidc | keys rotate saml
Signing keys.
.TP
.BI "enroll-link \-user " NAME
One-time second-factor enrollment link for an administrator (on the admin
listener when
.B server.admin_listen
is set; only that listener accepts it).
.TP
.BI "mfa reset \-user " NAME
Remove a user's second factor (local backend).
.TP
.B audit verify | audit export
Check or export the hash-chained audit log.
.TP
.BI gen-key " FILE"
Write a new 32-byte master key (mode 0600).
.TP
.B check
Validate the configuration and bind the service account.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-idp/idp.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-idp/credentials/
.B master-key
and
.BR ad-password ,
loaded by systemd.
.TP
.I /var/lib/conductor-idp/idp.db
State: clients, sealed signing keys, sessions, audit log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conductor (8),
.I /usr/share/doc/conductor-idp/README.Debian
